    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the others are the base and a helper), and it passes along with the full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires the create-owner response to carry `bulkSignupWarning: true` when more than 80 owners were already created today, else `false`. I implemented it following the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, keeping structural impact low:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly) to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it by name (no mapper change needed).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient boolean bulkSignupWarning` field with a plain getter/setter (two new one-line accessors, no existing method touched). It's transient, so no DB schema change and a freshly loaded owner (e.g. on GET) defaults to `false`.\n\n3. **`FlagBulkSignup.java`** (new small step) \u2014 counts existing owners registered today and sets the flag when `count > 80`, mirroring the existing `CheckDailyLimit` counting style. It runs before `SaveOwner`, so the count excludes the owner being created.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `flagBulkSignup` step into the pipeline (after `countNamesakes`, before `save`), under the same `transaction` governance as its neighbours.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`bulkSignupWarning` false on a fresh create, read back via GET) and the full build pass green.",
